{
  "$comment": "What a person might do, played on every screen size during All the Spaces' checks. Positions are fractions of the screen (0 to 1). Then the fishing: the rod (R), a cast (F does what the left mouse button does), the cooler (I). Escape closes the first-play guide if it has come up by then; the waits are long because a device without a graphics card plays it slowly. Then the weather, for the rain's, the lightning's and the hurricane's cost: the clock's menu (T) picks it (the checks play on their own, so a pick holds); it opens on its first button and the arrows move between its buttons, round from the last to the first (0 holds the clock, 1-4 rest until dawn, noon, dusk and night, 5 is the forecast, 6-15 calm to a hurricane, a southerly gale after the gale), Space takes one, and a rest jumps the clock, so the weather is all there at once instead of coming in over minutes. A shower (rain) at noon, a thunderstorm at dusk, then a hurricane picked at dusk: through its rain at night, three hours before its eye, and the next dawn, what it has torn and its wrack up the beach. The waits between presses let a slow frame take each one.",
